'''Dera Incarnon Genesis''' is an item that is used to add [[Incarnon]] upgrades to the {{Weapon|Dera}} or {{Weapon|Dera Vandal}}.

==Acquisition==
*Upon completion of [[The Duviri Paradox]] and [[Angels of the Zariman]], and unlocking [[The Steel Path]], players can earn {{Resource|Dera Incarnon Genesis}} from [[The Circuit]]'s Steel Path to place on their Dera with the help of [[Cavalero]] in the [[Chrysalith]]. This [[Incarnon Genesis]] form grants it evolutions to a transformation and newfound strength.
*Purchased from Cavalero for {{pc|120}}, complete with the resources used in its installation. This purchase can only be made '''once'''.

==Incarnon Genesis==

===Evolutions===
*Installing the Dera Incarnon Genesis requires 20 {{Resource|Pathos Clamp|Pathos Clamps}}, 80 {{Resource|Eevani}}, and 70 {{Resource|Ueymag}}.
*When installed, the first Evolution tier is unlocked. The following Evolution tiers, their requirements for unlocking them, and their related perks, are shown below;
**Each challenge additionally grants 5,000 [[affinity]] to the weapon, affected by [[Affinity Booster]]s.

====Evolution I====
*Weakpoint hits charge Incarnon Transmutation; Alt Fire transmutes. Switching back will expend any remaining charge.
*Fire high power beams and gain {{D|Magnetic}} Damage.
**Fires lasers that inflict {{D|Magnetic}} damage. Gains 3 [[Punch Through]] and [[Damage]], [[Critical Chance]], and [[Critical Multiplier]] are increased, but [[Status Chance]] and [[Fire Rate]] are lowered.
*Mode switching is '''not''' instantaneous and has an animation equal to the weapon's [[reload speed]].
*Incarnon Form is activated by filling the Incarnon Transmutation gauge that appears under the reticle by achieving [[Enemy Body Parts|weakpoint hits]] and then pressing the [[Alternate Fire]] button. '''25''' weakpoints will completely fill the gauge. A full gauge is not required to activate Incarnon Form.
**Charges do '''not''' generate on the backpacks of most [[MOA]] variants, or vulnerability spots generated by {{A|Sonar}} or {{M|Detect Vulnerability}} in places other than actual weakpoints.
**Weakpoints on corpses or [[Invulnerable]] targets do '''not''' build charges.
**Individual [[Multishot]] bullets can build charges.
*Instead of drawing ammunition from its reserves, the Dera's Incarnon Form uses a separate "magazine" with each charge producing '''2''' rounds to a maximum of '''50'''. Once all ammunition is expended, the Dera reverts to its normal form.
**Incarnon Form's magazine is '''not''' affected by mods.
**Incarnon Form is '''not''' affected by [[Ammo Efficiency]] (such as {{A|Energized Munitions}}).
**Charges and Incarnon Form persists through all activities, such as holstering, [[bleedout]], or being [[disarm]]ed. However, charges and Incarnon Form are removed upon [[death]].
*Swapping to and from Incarnon Form will fully reload the normal form's magazine.

====Evolution II====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Complete a solo mission with this weapon equipped.
*Perk 1: '''Crimson Overture:'''
**Increase Base Damage by '''+8''' (Dera) / '''+6''' (Vandal)
**On Kill: '''+20%''' [[Ammo Efficiency]] for '''5s'''. Stacks up to '''4x'''.
*Perk 2: '''Paragon Essence:'''
**Increase Base Damage by '''+6''' (Dera) / '''+4''' (Vandal)
**On Status Effect: '''+5%''' [[Fire Rate]] for '''5s'''. Stacks up to '''6x'''.

====Evolution III====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Kill '''100''' enemies with this weapon's Incarnon Form.
*Perk 1: '''Swift Deliverance:'''
**'''+50%''' [[Projectile Speed]]
*Perk 2: '''Extended Volley:'''
**Increase Base [[Magazine Capacity]] by '''+22''' (Dera) / '''+30''' (Vandal)
*Perk 3: '''Evolved Autoloader:'''
**'''+50%''' [[Magazine]] Reloaded/s when [[Holster]]ed

====Evolution IV====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Kill '''30''' enemies afflicted with '''4''' or more Status Effects.
**{{Arcane|Secondary Encumber}}, {{WF|Voruna}}'s {{A|Fangs of Raksh}}, {{WF|Citrine}}'s {{A|Fractured Blast}} and {{A|Prismatic Gem}}, and {{WF|Koumei}}'s Passive, {{A|Kumihimo}} and {{A|Bunraku}} are effective at spreading numerous status effects. Consider reducing {{Stat|Ability Strength}} so these abilities do not take away Dera's kills.
*Perk 1: '''Deathtrap Trigger:'''
**Increase Base [[Critical Chance]] by '''+14%'''
**Increase Base [[Critical Damage]] Multiplier by '''+0.6x''' (Dera) / '''+0.4x''' (Vandal)
*Perk 2: '''High Ground:'''
**Increase Base [[Critical Chance]] by '''25%''' of current [[Status Chance]], up to '''35%'''.
***For Non-Incarnon Dera Vandal, +366.7% Status Chance is needed to max out the Critical Chance bonus. It can be easily achieved with [[Primary Crux]].
***For Incarnon Dera Vandal and Non-Incarnon Dera, +536.4% Status Chance is needed to max out the Critical Chance bonus.
*Perk 3: '''Elemental Balance:'''
**Increase Base [[Status Chance]] by '''+18%''' (Dera) / '''+14%''' (Vandal)

==Notes==
* Incarnon transformation doesn't override equipped skins

